A3 (ring edges strict only inside the 60 m body gate) — THE DRAG
HYPOTHESIS IS CONFIRMED AT HECA AND REFUTED AT SPJC.  within_shape airside
by chord (<= 60 m / > 60 m):
    HECA  battery 765/519   staged 1319/961   A3 1044/1063
    SPJC  battery  45/0     staged   76/24    A3   80/40
  HECA's SHORT class fell 1319 -> 1044 (-21 %) and its worst row 11.59 ->
  9.59 m: relaxing the long constraints DID stop them dragging the short
  ones.  SPJC's short class did not move and its long class grew.
  A fifth arm says STILL NOT ONE VIOLATION AT 5 % (HECA 2055 @1.0 % + 52
  @1.5 %; SPJC 106 @1.0 % + 14 @1.5 %).
  THE 20 WORST ARE THE CLASS A3 TARGETED AND DID NOT REACH: way -10612,
  cap 1.0 %, 1.09-1.26 %, |de| 8.36-9.59 m, chords 665-857 m.  They now
  arrive through the SPINE door, not the cover door — the ``spine_caps``
  carve-out this lane flagged when implementing A3.  Evidence:
  apron_seniority marks 2,712 of 3,288 HECA apron nodes SENIOR; pair_caps
  still carries 9,782 unified:apron rows on chords > 60 m, longest 1,417 m
  at an implied 1.50 %.  Whether a long APRON spine pair should take the
  length gate is the open question, and it decides HECA.
  CYXY's A3 body sha is IDENTICAL to the staged arm — no long ring edge
  there, so A3 is a no-op.

THE MECHANISM WORKS AND DOES NOT PAY.  Three findings, in order of weight.

1. *** THE PRECEDENCE HOLDS EXACTLY: senior nodes MOVED in A2 = 0 on all
   three airports. ***  The spec's own STOP condition is not tripped; the
   freeze covers the sweeps AND the band clamp.  Flag-off is proven
   byte-for-byte on CYXY: O4_APRON_STAGED_SOLVE=0 rebuilds body_sha
   40617f978f7a, exactly compose-v3's (twin (c) on a real airport).

2. *** A1'S BOTH-HARD RESIDUE IS ESSENTIALLY NIL, WHICH REFUTES THE
   SPEC'S OWN PREMISE. ***  Section 4 expected A1's both-hard count to be
   "the honest pin-contradiction number" and the top-20 to be the next
   round's brief.  Measured:
     CYXY  1 row,  worst 0.055 m  (runway-datum / runway-datum)
     SPJC 26 rows, worst 0.006 m  (unified:apron, terrain / terrain)
     HECA  4 rows, worst 0.446 m  (unified:junction, runway-datum both ends)
   THE PINS DO NOT CONTRADICT THE MOVEMENT-SURFACE LAW.  A1's over_cap is
   large (HECA 4309, SPJC 324, CYXY 4) while its BOTH-HARD is 4/26/1, so
   the senior law is FEASIBLE and the residue is ordinary unconverged
   projection, not a pin contradiction.  There is no pin docket to hand on.

3. *** THE STAGED SOLVE CANNOT MOVE THE NUMBER BECAUSE THE SENIOR SET IS
   ALMOST THE WHOLE APRON. ***  Interior movers vs seniors re-frozen in A2:
     CYXY 114 movers / 272 seniors      (of 33,360 nodes)
     SPJC 355 movers / 2,195 seniors    (of 63,696)
     HECA 334 movers / 1,506 seniors    (of 139,459)
   Under A2's predicates 82-86 % of the interior-pair endpoints are
   already movement surfaces, so A2 has almost nothing to move and
   precedence has almost nothing to protect.  CYXY's sidecar partition
   says the same in the large: 287 senior / 206 interior of 493 apron ring
   nodes.  A mechanism that reorders two sets cannot help when one of them
   is nearly empty.

WHERE THE DEBT ACTUALLY SITS, unchanged from v2/v3 and now measured a
fourth time: NOT ONE VIOLATION ON ANY AIRPORT, IN ANY ARM, IS PRICED AT
THE 5 % CAP.  Staged within_shape airside by cap — CYXY 2 @1.0 %; SPJC
89 @1.0 % + 11 @1.5 %; HECA 2176 @1.0 % + 104 @1.5 %.  HECA's accumulated
excess on the strict class went 4332 (battery) -> 7622 pct-points.

SPJC RESIDUAL, split per spec section 8: within_shape airside 100 (45
battery), of which 25 are within 1.10x of cap and 58 are >2x — and 42 of
those 58 are chords <= 5 m, i.e. THE WELD CLUSTER at
(-12.021394,-77.110990) where ways -10113 / -10162 / -10698 / -10699 meet.
That is a seat/weld docket item, not this lane's.  transverse 41 is the
best of any arm (battery 46); drainage_spine, strip_arc and
strip_longitudinal are unchanged from the battery.

